Q1 — Tile 1.4: Coverage quality (hosts vs services per app)

The earlier A4 query showed that service tags are an array, just like host tags. So this version uses expand tags directly instead of the splitString workaround I gave you before.

fetch dt.entity.host
| fields id, tags, tagStr = toString(tags)
| filter contains(lower(tagStr), "portfolio:claims")
| expand tag = tags
| filter contains(tag, "APMID:") or contains(tag, "APPID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = if(contains(tag, "APMID:"), splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1],
                    else: splitString(tag, "APPID:")[1])
| filter startsWith(apmid, "APP")
| summarize hosts = countDistinctExact(id), by:{apmid}
| lookup [
    fetch dt.entity.service
    | fields id, tags
    | expand tag = tags
    | filter contains(tag, "APMID:") or contains(tag, "APPID:")
    | fieldsAdd apmid = if(contains(tag, "APMID:"), splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1],
                        else: splitString(tag, "APPID:")[1])
    | filter startsWith(apmid, "APP")
    | summarize services = countDistinctExact(id), by:{apmid}
  ], sourceField: apmid, lookupField: apmid, prefix: "s."
| fieldsAdd services = coalesce(s.services, 0)
| fieldsAdd coverage = if(services >= 5, "Full stack",
                       else: if(services > 0, "Thin",
                       else: "Host only - no app visibility"))
| summarize apps = count(), by:{coverage}


What to check: the three counts should add up to 187. Before the final summarize, you can also add | sort services desc and remove the last line to see the per-app rows.

